  "original_source_text": "Sparse Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) models can outperform dense LLMs at similar computation, but their large expert parameters create high memory demand, making single-GPU deployment difficult. Offloading addresses this by storing inactive experts on CPU, yet static caches ignore dynamic routing and existing predictors for expert usage are often inaccurate or costly. We present ExpertFlow, a lightweight MoE inference system with a routing path predictor, a routing-aware token scheduler, and a predictive expert cache. Together, these components enable efficient expert loading and execution, reducing GPU memory by 93.72% and improving throughput by up to 10× on a single GPU.",
